--- !u!114 &1413275575
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1413275573}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f09c7de40bd1bec4e9665d48248bab18, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  text: "This scene will work if the Universal Rendering Pipeline is enabled.\r\n\r\nYou
    can add post processes on the renderer using the \u201CAdd Render\u201D button.\r\n\r\nThere
    are already some nice ones configured on the renderer in the folder PostProcessingDithering/URP/PipelineAssets
    that you can hook up to the pipeline asset. You can play with the effects by
    enabling or disabling different features.\r\n\n--------------------\nExample
    Tips\n--------------------\n\n\u26A0\uFE0F The Dither Texture Bias examples are
    best viewed at 1920\xD71080.\r\n\u26A0\uFE0F Disable the Pixelate Object when
    enabling the Dither Texture Bias or UV Mapped examples.\r\n\u26A0\uFE0F The Min
    filter is used to make dark lines thicker. Disable it if you disable the outline,
    or use the Max filter if you want to make a light outline thicker.\r\n\u26A0\uFE0F
    It is better not to have more than one tone map active.\r\n\u26A0\uFE0F It is
    not usual to have so many map renderers.\r\n\u26A0\uFE0F Blurring does not improve
    most dithering schemes, except the two \u201CMarks\u201D examples (switch off
    the outline and Min filter in that case).\r"
